<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Turing k_c at 492 nm for the 18-file Eldredgeops eye (Pass 2) (Eldredgeops rana_18file)",
        "Turing k_c at 492 nm for the 18-file Eldredgeops eye (Pass 2) faithfully reproduces Eldredgeops rana_18file morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Eldredgeops rana_18file specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Eldredgeops rana_18file" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A cryptographic nanopublication signature.",
        "does_not_claim: That file loss retunes k_c.",
        "does_not_claim: That the Schnakenberg coefficients are Devonian biochemistry.",
        "does_not_claim: That the eye photograph is a PDE solution or that Pearson r = 1 is a pixel fit.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Gamma sweep showing lambda proportional to gamma^(-1/2), and an equal-diffusion field.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Linear wavelength fixed at 492 nm = 4.915e-07 m for the 18-file morph at 387 Ma.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Otsu mask, radial-spectrum KS, and three-seed FFT wavelength on the Commons photograph.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Wavelengths per file increase by 18/17 if the arc is conserved and one file is lost by 384 Ma.",
        "reported_in_source: Clarkson, Levi-Setti and Horváth 2006 describe the schizochroal calcite eye.",
        "reported_in_source: Eldredge 1972 documents the Middle Devonian file-count series for Phacops rana.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 states the two-species reaction used here.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 states the diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: 492 nm is the assigned detail scale, not an Eldredge measurement.",
        "transfer_boundary: The photograph is Eldredgeops rana, not a proven Cazenovian 18-file voucher." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Eldredgeops rana_18file (Middle Devonian (Cazenovian, 387 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Eldredgeops" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/eldredgeops_rana_18file_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Eldredgeops rana_18file; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 states the diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979 states the two-species reaction used here. | Eldredge 1972 documents the Middle Devonian file-count series for Phacops rana. | Clarkson, Levi-Setti and Horváth 2006 describe the schizochroal calcite eye.; reconstructed_in_script: Linear wavelength fixed at 492 nm = 4.915e-07 m for the 18-file morph at 387 Ma. | Gamma sweep showing lambda proportional to gamma^(-1/2), and an equal-diffusion field. | Otsu mask, radial-spectrum KS, and three-seed FFT wavelength on the Commons photograph. | Wavelengths per file increase by 18/17 if the arc is conserved and one file is lost by 384 Ma.; transfer_boundary: 492 nm is the assigned detail scale, not an Eldredge measurement. | The photograph is Eldredgeops rana, not a proven Cazenovian 18-file voucher.; does_not_claim: That the Schnakenberg coefficients are Devonian biochemistry. | That the eye photograph is a PDE solution or that Pearson r = 1 is a pixel fit. | That file loss retunes k_c. | A cryptographic nanopublication signature.]; other sources: Systematics and evolution of Phacops rana (Green, 1832) and Phacops iowensis Delo, 1935 <https://digitallibrary.amnh.org/handle/2246/1095>; phenomenon_size: 357 nm (3.57e-07 m, log10=-6.447 m, tier=2_macromolecular_100nm); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 357 nm to 803 µm): 357 nm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-bioelectric-polarity, 1.1 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-vertex-packing, 18 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-turing-wavelength, 36 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-clock-wavefront, 80 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-morphogen-condensation, 98 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-elastic-buckling, 112 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-flux-canalization, 156 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-branching-tree" ;
